# CAPTURE OWNERSHIP, the REFCOUNT-HANDLE cell of the typed axis.
#
# `Shared[T]` is a thin refcount handle: `copy_semantics` is `Trivial`, so it is
# NOT `is_resource_type` and no deep clone exists for it — its "clone" is a
# by-value incref. Every consuming-position pass that only asks
# "is this a resource?" walks straight past it, which is how a handle ends up
# shallow-aliased into an environment, and how an environment ends up declaring
# a drop strategy that does not match what it actually holds.
#
# ⚠ WHAT THIS CELL IS FOR, stated honestly: it is GREEN before the
# capture-ownership rule lands as well as after. It is here because a draft of
# that rule that asked only `is_resource_type` broke exactly this shape, and the
# environment's computed drop strategy is what caught it. A cell that guards a
# prospective break is worth as much as one that pins a fixed bug, but it is a
# different claim and should not be read as the second.
#
# ⚠ SCOPE OMITTED, AND THE REASON GIVEN HERE WAS FALSE (corrected 2026-09-04).
# This header used to say the ESCAPING variant of this cell was "not reachable —
# a returned NAMED closure capturing a local is rejected by
# `E_ClosureEscapesScope` whatever it captures". It is reachable, and a
# PRE-EXISTING fixture already sits on it: `tests/fixtures/shared_callable.gg`
# reaches it through `Shared[Callable[int()]]((): counter.get() + 1)`, which
# builds green — the escape diagnostic keys on the SPELLING (a local AND named
# closure), not on escape, which is `todo/t1068`.
# ⇒ THE ESCAPING CELL IS GENUINELY UNCOVERED HERE, not covered-by-impossibility,
# and it is the cell that regressed: `shared_callable` went from 16 B/1 to
# 56 B/3 under `--sanitize` when the capture site began materialising, because
# the `Shared` box now moves into an env field nothing drops (`todo/t1210`).
# A typed axis whose "impossible" value has a live fixture sitting on it is a
# hole in the net, not an omission (Core #12).
#
# INTENDED: prints `7`, `9`, `7`, rc 0, both backends, no double-decrement.

from std.sync import Shared

void main():
    Shared[int] cell = Shared[int](7)
    Callable[int()] read = (): cell.get()
    Callable[int()] read_plus = (): cell.get() + 2
    print(read())
    print(read_plus())
    print(cell.get())
